  "date": "10 May 1796, afternoon",
  "blurb": "Beaulieu's army is falling back across the Adda after Bonaparte marched round its flank. Its rearguard under Sebottendorf stands on the east bank behind fourteen guns, with the wooden bridge, some two hundred yards long, in front of it. The French have been in Lodi since the morning; their guns have been firing along the bridge all afternoon. About six o'clock the carabiniers are to go out of the gate and over it.",
